#*:Miss Pross, exploring the depths of her '''reticule''' through her tears with great difficulty, paid for her wine.
#*{{quote-book|lang=en|year=1993|publisher=Penguin|year_published=1994|author=TC Boyle|authorlink=TC Boyle|title=The Road to Wellville|page=150|passage=Eleanor wore a green silk dress to bring out here eyes, with an ivory tatted collar and '''reticule''' to match.}}
#* '''2006''', Thomas Pynchon, ''Against the Day'', Vintage 2007, p. 606,<sup>[https://books.google.ca/books?id=iBA0e-8kZ4cC&printsec=frontcover#v=onepage&q&f=false]</sup>
